        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(mcp): suppress unhandled rejection from async gateway event handler",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `onEvent` callback in `OpenClawChannelBridge` calls `void this.handleGatewayEvent(event)` without a `.catch()` handler. Since `handleGatewayEvent` is async and can reject, this creates an unhandled promise rejection that crashes the MCP gateway process.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdd a noop `.catch(() => {})` to suppress the unhandled rejection, matching the pattern used elsewhere in the codebase for fire-and-forget async callbacks.\n\n## User Impact\n\nPrevents the gateway from crashing when an MCP channel bridge event handler throws.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Behavior\nThe `onEvent` callback now attaches a `.catch(() => {})` to the fire-and-forget `handleGatewayEvent(event)` promise.\n\n### Source\n`src/mcp/channel-bridge.ts:151`\n```ts\nonEvent: (event) => {\n  void this.handleGatewayEvent(event).catch(() => {});\n},\n```\n\n### Test output\n```\n$ pnpm test -- src/mcp/channel-bridge.test.ts --run\n[test] starting test/vitest/vitest.unit.config.ts\n ✓ |unit| src/mcp/channel-bridge.test.ts (16 tests) 312ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  16 passed (16)\n   Duration  1.83s\n\n[test] passed 1 Vitest shard in 14.16s\n```\n\n### Notes\n- This is a defensive fix; the callback is fire-and-forget by design.\n- The `.catch(() => {})` pattern is already used elsewhere for similar fire-and-forget handlers.\n- Existing tests continue to pass.",
        "branch": "fix/channel-bridge-void-async-catch",
